  "program": {
    "module": {
      "summary": "Pensions Act 2008 s.3 — employer automatic-enrolment duty.\n\ns.3(1): a jobholder is in scope if (a) aged 22+, (b) below pensionable\nage, and (c) paid more than £10,000 in the relevant pay reference period\n(pro-rated per s.3(6B)).\ns.3(3)-(4): no duty if already an active qualifying-scheme member, or if\nthe jobholder recently opted out within the prescribed lookback.\n\n`current_age_years`, `pensionable_age_years`,\n`active_member_of_qualifying_scheme`, `recently_opted_out` and\n`earnings_this_prp` are caller-supplied facts. The lookback window and\nthe PA 1995 Sch 4 pensionable-age test sit outside this RuleSpec module."
    },
